      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-341153",
      ":question/problem": "$F(x) = {1, \\mid x \u2208 [0, 1); x, \\mid x \u2208 [- 1, 0)$\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x \u2208 [- 1, 1)$.\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x \u2208 (-1, 1)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x \u2208 (-1, 1)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | $lim_(x \u2192 - 1^{+})F(x) = lim_(x \u2192 1^{-})F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |"
